# Destination secrets for `kamal ... -d ovh` ONLY.
#
# Kamal 2 loads ["<path>-common", "<path>.<destination>"], i.e. for -d ovh it reads
# `.kamal/secrets-common` (shared: RAILS_MASTER_KEY, CHUNK_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, registry token, …)
# PLUS this file. The apex/base deploy loads `.kamal/secrets-common` + `.kamal/secrets` and never
# touches this file, so the `op read`s below run ONLY on OVH deploys.
#
# This file is safe for git: it holds NO raw secrets, only 1Password references resolved at deploy
# time. DO NOT paste PEM contents here.
#
# Cloudflare Origin certificate for tinkerex.com (Cloudflare dashboard -> SSL/TLS -> Origin Server
# -> Create Certificate; hostnames `tinkerex.com` + `*.tinkerex.com`). Store the two PEM blocks in
# a 1Password item and point the refs below at it. Adjust the vault/item/field names to match what
# you create (these mirror the existing op:// pattern used for the SeaweedFS keys).
TINKEREX_ORIGIN_CERT_PEM=$(op read "op://Personal/tinkerex-origin/certificate")
TINKEREX_ORIGIN_KEY_PEM=$(op read "op://Personal/tinkerex-origin/private key")
